# Engineering

- Tests: `cd iTantra && ./gradlew :core:test`. Language loops use `Language.entries`, not “three languages.”
- Changing PTT, receive, LID, packs, or `Language` requires `:core` tests.
- Do not invent WER, RTF, RAM, latency, or APK size. See `iTantra/docs/MEASUREMENTS.md`.
- Do not bundle huge ONNX files into git. Paths and pack manager are enough until weights exist.
- Out of scope unless asked: alert UI, diagnostics screen, call mode, mesh, OTA store, fake eval tables.

Adding a language: enum + new wire code + lexicons + (optional) dictionary pairs. Registry/UI are enum-driven.
